assign the values to matrix Sigma to make it has off-diagonal blocks as follows (only show the first 20 columns and rows):<div><br> \r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\"><u></u> <u></u></span><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mZTaybXW92g/U9pwMJlg0CI/AAAAAAAAB6g/z9Lhws2IrdA/s1600/a.png\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mZTaybXW92g/U9pwMJlg0CI/AAAAAAAAB6g/z9Lhws2IrdA/s1600/a.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466130326000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00hBN6JFOgLTVheZ0BxbLa\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mZTaybXW92g/U9pwMJlg0CI/AAAAAAAAB6g/z9Lhws2IrdA/s1600/a.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I used this code (kind of R algorithm) in the Model block:<br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;\">  for(g in 1:35){</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\">     \r\nfor (i in RR[g,1]:RR[g,2]) {<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\">     \r\nfor (j in RR[g,1]:RR[g,2]) {<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\">        \r\nSigma[i,j] &lt;- 1<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\">     \r\n}<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:blue\">     \r\n}<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;line-height:18px\">RR[g,1]</span> can be automatically promote vectors to reals, but it doesn&#39;t work for RStan.\r\n\r\n<br>I’m wondering how to specify a particular row and column in a matrix, like RR[1, 1].  In particular, how to create the matrix Sigma as above.<div><br></div><div>My Stan code: (please don&#39;t worry too much about the code other than the assigning the matrix part)</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">data {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">int&lt;lower=1&gt; N;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">vector[N] x;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">vector[N] y;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">matrix[35,2] RR;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">transformed data {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">vector[N] mu;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">for (i in 1:N) mu[i] &lt;- 0;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">parameters {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">real&lt;lower=0&gt; s1;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">real&lt;lower=0&gt; l1;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">real&lt;lower=0&gt; l2;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">real&lt;lower=0&gt; s2;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">real&lt;lower=0&gt; sigma_sq;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">model {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">matrix[N,N] Sigma;</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">// off-diagonal elements</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">for (i in 1:(N-1)) {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">for (j in (i+1):N) {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">Sigma[i,j] &lt;- s1 * exp(-0.5 * pow((x[i] - x[j])/l1,2));</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">for(g in 1:35){</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">                for (i in RR[g,1]:RR[g,2]) {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">                for (j in RR[g,1]:RR[g,2]) {</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">                Sigma[i,j] &lt;-x[i,j]</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">      }</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">      }</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">// diagonal elements</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">for (k in 1:N)</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">Sigma[k,k] &lt;- s1 + sigma_sq; // + jitter</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">s1 ~ cauchy(0,5);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">l1 ~ normal(20,3);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">s2 ~ cauchy(0,5);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">l2 ~ cauchy(0,5);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">sigma_sq ~ cauchy(0,5);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">y ~ multi_normal(mu,Sigma);</font></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#0000ff\">}</font></p></div></blockquote><div>Thanks for any comments!</div></div><div><br></div><div>Dora</div></div>"
    ]
